//@version=6
// MTF Liquidity Dealing Range
//
// Layer 1 - liquidity register.
//   Sources: up to 5 MTF swing slots, 3 sessions, optional PDH/PDL.
//   Only sources at or above the chart timeframe are used. No promotion.
//   Levels anchor at the chart bar that actually printed the wick.
//   Levels merge on a tick tolerance and union their tags; quotas are
//   enforced per tag, so a level tagged 1h+4h keeps its 4h life when the
//   1h quota ages it out.
//   Sweep is by wick, touch counts, on confirmed bars only.
//
// Layer 2 - dealing range.
//   No range exists until liquidity has framed one. The first registered
//   purge opens one side; the opposing purge completes the pair. Only then
//   is the range valid. The tracking side follows its excursion extreme.
//   Two engines read the same purges and can be shown together:
//     Rotation - any opposing purge re-anchors that side. The original engine.
//     IPDA Frame - once framed, only a purge at or beyond a boundary moves it,
//                and a purge only ever widens it. Internal sweeps are
//                repricing. It contracts on time alone: no boundary may be
//                older than the IPDA lookback of 20, 40 or 60 Daily bars.
//   Delivery - its own toggle. A raid, then a confirmed close through the
//     last opposing chart-TF swing. Raid extreme to displacement extreme.
//   One primary range feeds everything downstream, including the
//   premium / discount box.
//
// Revision notes
//   - REVERSAL: premium / discount display reinstated, as a box split at
//     0.5 only. This reverses the earlier removal of premium / discount
//     shading as redundant.
//   - Refinement ("most energetic swing") removed. Group 6 is now the
//     delivery range.
//   - Manual range. A fourth primary range, picked by time the way
//     Dealing Range Liquidity Reversal's Dated DR is: its high and low are
//     the highest high and lowest low between two times, anchored at the
//     candles that made them. It does not move when price trades beyond
//     it. The automatic ranges keep running and can be switched back to.
//   - Value area. The range-anchored profile now marks VAH and VAL: the
//     band around the POC holding 70% of the volume traded inside the
//     range. Optional real volume at price from TradingView's footprint
//     (Premium and up), off by default; bars without footprint data fall
//     back to the even spread. Footprint request pattern after ata_sabanci's
//     Volume Footprint (MPL-2.0).
//   - CME clock. A perpetual that mirrors a CME market (trade.xyz,
//     Binance CL) is read as the futures contract would print it on an
//     intraday chart: candles from Friday 17:00 to Sunday 18:00 New York
//     and in the daily 17:00-18:00 halt are ignored. They sweep nothing,
//     move no range, start no session and print no swing. The day runs
//     18:00 to 17:00 New York, and PDH / PDL come from that day. Same
//     symbol list and setting name as Dealing Range Liquidity Reversal.
//   - Ranging removed. Detecting consolidation from swings and ATR could
//     not tell a range from a trend reliably enough to gate sweeps, so
//     every registered sweep now reaches the range engines. The table is
//     group 10.
//   - Frame capped by an IPDA lookback. Without it a widen-only frame
//     converged on the whole loaded history. Delivery moved to its own
//     toggle in group 6.
//   - Review fixes: a bar that takes both sides frames what it proves and
//     suspends direction; primary falls back to a LIVE range; IPDA
//     contraction waits for a full window; a contraction no longer reports
//     as a liquidity reframe; Draw reached tests the pool that was the
//     draw before the bar; wick cache 24.
//   - Volume profile placement: profile gap and profile width are independent.
//     The histogram is anchored outside the primary range's right edge, so
//     changing its width no longer drags it back over price or the P/D box.
//   - The first complete pair fires Framed only, never Framed and Reframed
//     together. Draw reached fires only when the exact registered pool that
//     was the draw is swept - not when it is cleared by a day reset or
//     trimmed by a quota.
//
// Layer 3 - equilibrium, position, draw, table, alerts.
//
// Layer 5 - volume context. Optional. A volume profile binned by
//   ATR and anchored to the live dealing range, plus the POC. Volume
//   is spread across every row a bar's high-low range touches, so the
//   node is where contracts changed hands, not where closes clustered.
//   Not an ICT construct. It answers one question the range cannot:
//   where the bulk of the business sits relative to equilibrium.
//
// Layer 4 - odds. Optional. Every live level is priced as a first
//   passage probability, p = 1/(1+k), k being its distance in R.
//   This is the driftless baseline: the odds of touching a target
//   before a 1R stop when there is no edge at all. It detects
//   nothing and predicts nothing. Its only use is as the number
//   your read has to beat.

indicator("MTF Liquidity Dealing Range", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_polylines_count = 100, max_boxes_count = 50, max_bars_back = 2000)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Types
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

type Level
    float  p
    bool   hi
    int    x        // origin time - the bar that printed the wick
    int    born
    string tags     // pipe delimited
    bool   swept
    int    sx       // sweep time
    line   ln
    label  lb
    label  tx

type Sess
    float h
    float l
    int   hx
    int   lx

type Track
    int   op
    float h
    float l
    int   hx
    int   lx
    array<int> ops
    array<int> hxs
    array<int> lxs

// a dealing-range engine: two boundaries, the side being tracked,
// and this bar's events
type Rng
    float hi
    int   hiT
    int   hiB
    bool  hiSet = false
    float lo
    int   loT
    int   loB
    bool  loSet = false
    int   st = 0            // +1 tracking the high, -1 tracking the low
    bool  amb = false       // sequence unknown after a double sweep
    bool  reframed = false
    bool  extended = false
    bool  contracted = false

// the delivery range: a raid arms it, a close through structure forms it
type Dlv
    int   pend = 0          // -1 armed after a buy-side raid, +1 after a sell-side raid
    float pExt              // raid extreme while armed
    int   pExtT
    int   pExtB
    float pOpp              // opposite extreme since the raid
    int   pOppT
    int   pOppB
    float pMss              // the swing a close must break
    int   dir = 0           // -1 bearish delivery, +1 bullish, 0 none
    float hi
    int   hiT
    int   hiB
    float lo
    int   loT
    int   loB
    bool  formed = false
    bool  extended = false

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Inputs
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

gSrc = "1. Timeframes"
levelsN = input.int(3, "Levels", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gSrc, tooltip = "Unswept levels kept per tag, per side.")
mtfLen  = input.int(2, "Swing length", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = gSrc)

src1On = input.bool(true,  "TF 1", inline = "t1", group = gSrc)
src1Tf = input.timeframe("60",  "", inline = "t1", group = gSrc)
src2On = input.bool(true,  "TF 2", inline = "t2", group = gSrc)
src2Tf = input.timeframe("240", "", inline = "t2", group = gSrc)
src3On = input.bool(true,  "TF 3", inline = "t3", group = gSrc)
src3Tf = input.timeframe("D",   "", inline = "t3", group = gSrc)
src4On = input.bool(false, "TF 4", inline = "t4", group = gSrc)
src4Tf = input.timeframe("W",   "", inline = "t4", group = gSrc)
src5On = input.bool(false, "TF 5", inline = "t5", group = gSrc)
src5Tf = input.timeframe("15",  "", inline = "t5", group = gSrc)

gSess = "2. Sessions"
s1On   = input.bool(true, "", inline = "s1", group = gSess)
s1Name = input.string("Asia", "", inline = "s1", group = gSess)
s1Time = input.session("2000-0000", "", inline = "s1", group = gSess)
s1Col  = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "", inline = "s1", group = gSess)

s2On   = input.bool(true, "", inline = "s2", group = gSess)
s2Name = input.string("London", "", inline = "s2", group = gSess)
s2Time = input.session("0200-0500", "", inline = "s2", group = gSess)
s2Col  = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "", inline = "s2", group = gSess)

s3On   = input.bool(false, "", inline = "s3", group = gSess)
s3Name = input.string("New York", "", inline = "s3", group = gSess)
s3Time = input.session("0930-1200", "", inline = "s3", group = gSess)
s3Col  = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "", inline = "s3", group = gSess)

gDay = "3. Daily levels"
pdOn       = input.bool(true,  "PDH / PDL", inline = "d", group = gDay, tooltip = "Taken from the symbol's completed Daily bar, so it agrees with what a Daily chart shows. On the CME clock, taken from the previous CME day, 18:00 to 17:00 New York.")
pdCol      = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "", inline = "d", group = gDay)
dailyReset = input.bool(false, "Daily reset", group = gDay, tooltip = "Clear every level when the Daily bar rolls. Off clears only session and PDH/PDL levels.")
cmeClockOn = input.bool(true, "Hold perpetual futures to the CME clock", group = gDay, tooltip = "Applies only to perpetual futures that mirror a CME market (every trade.xyz / HIP3XYZ market, BINANCE:CLUSDT.P), and only on intraday charts. On: candles from Friday 17:00 to Sunday 18:00 New York and in the daily 17:00-18:00 halt are ignored, as on the futures contract. They sweep no level, move no range, build no session and print no swing. The day runs 18:00 to 17:00 New York, so the daily roll, PDH / PDL and the IPDA day count follow CME. Off: the perpetual is read 24/7 on its own daily bar. Futures charts are never affected.")

gStyle = "4. Register style"
lblSize     = input.string("Small", "Pane labels", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = gStyle)
colMtf      = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "Levels", inline = "c1", group = gStyle)
regWidth    = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "c1", group = gStyle)
regStyle    = input.string("Solid", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], inline = "c1", group = gStyle)
showHistory = input.bool(true, "History", inline = "h", group = gStyle, tooltip = "Keep swept levels on the chart, terminated at their sweep bar and always drawn dotted. The colour and count on this row apply only when this is on.")
historyN    = input.int(3, "", minval = 1, maxval = 100, inline = "h", group = gStyle)
colSwept    = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "", inline = "h", group = gStyle)
showRegister = input.bool(true, "Show register", group = gStyle)
showOrigin  = input.bool(true,  "Origin labels", inline = "v", group = gStyle)
showMarker  = input.bool(false, "Pending markers", inline = "v", group = gStyle)
maxDistAtr  = input.float(0, "Hide beyond (x ATR)", minval = 0, maxval = 50, step = 0.5, group = gStyle, tooltip = "0 draws every level. Otherwise levels further than this many ATR from price are hidden until price approaches.")
mergeTicks  = input.int(2, "Merge tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, maxval = 50, group = gStyle, tooltip = "A merged tag set should mean the same structural price, not merely nearby swings. Keep this tight.")

gRange = "5. Dealing range"
rotOn   = input.bool(true,  "Rotation range", group = gRange, tooltip = "The original engine. Any opposing registered purge re-anchors that side at the purging bar, so a retracement that takes internal liquidity re-anchors the range to that rotation.")
frameOn = input.bool(false, "IPDA Frame", inline = "fr", group = gRange)
ipdaLb  = input.int(20, "IPDA lookback (days)", options = [20, 40, 60], inline = "fr", group = gRange, tooltip = "IPDA Frame: external context, not a second dealing range. Framed the same way as Rotation, but once both sides are set only a purge of a pool at or beyond a boundary moves it, and a purge only widens it. Internal sweeps are repricing. It contracts on time: any boundary older than the lookback is re-anchored to that side's extreme inside the window, at the bar that printed it. The window is the current Daily bar plus the previous lookback-1, recalculated every day, so it agrees with the same count on a Daily chart. Until the chart holds a full window of Daily bars, no contraction happens and the frame is marked not ready with the days actually loaded - a 60D frame is never silently computed on fewer days.")
primSel = input.string("Rotation", "Primary range", options = ["Rotation", "IPDA Frame", "Delivery", "Manual"], group = gRange, tooltip = "The range the box, EQ, position, draw marker, boundary odds, volume profile, table and alerts all measure against. The primary draws solid with the labels below; any other range that is on draws quieter. If the chosen range is not live, it falls back to the first LIVE range in the order Rotation, IPDA Frame, Delivery, and the table marks the fallback. Manual is your own range, set by the two times below.")
manFrom = input.time(timestamp("2026-10-19T18:00:00-04:00"), "Manual from", group = gRange, active = primSel == "Manual", tooltip = "Manual range: its high and low are the highest high and lowest low from the candle holding the first time through the candle holding the second, both included, anchored at the candles that made them. Pick the low's candle and the high's candle and both are in. The pickers follow TradingView's date convention, which may not be New York time: after setting them, check the range lines start on the candles you meant. While the second time is still ahead the range keeps growing; after it, the range is fixed and does not move when price trades beyond it. On the CME clock, candles while CME is shut are skipped. A start older than the loaded history begins at the first loaded candle.")
manTo   = input.time(timestamp("2026-10-20T17:00:00-04:00"), "Manual to", group = gRange, active = primSel == "Manual")
showHi = input.bool(true, "Range high", inline = "rh", group = gRange)
colHi  = input.color(#2962FF, "", inline = "rh", group = gRange)
txtHi  = input.string("DR HIGH", "", inline = "rh", group = gRange)
widHi  = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "rh", group = gRange)

showLo = input.bool(true, "Range low", inline = "rl", group = gRange)
colLo  = input.color(#F23645, "", inline = "rl", group = gRange)
txtLo  = input.string("DR LOW", "", inline = "rl", group = gRange)
widLo  = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "rl", group = gRange)

showEq = input.bool(true, "Equilibrium", inline = "eq", group = gRange)
colEq  = input.color(#787B86, "", inline = "eq", group = gRange)
txtEq  = input.string("DR EQ", "", inline = "eq", group = gRange)
widEq  = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "eq", group = gRange)
showPrice  = input.bool(true, "Show price on labels", group = gRange)
extendBars = input.int(12, "Extend right (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = gRange)
edgeTrigger = input.bool(false, "Boundary violation counts as a purge", group = gRange, tooltip = "Off: only a registered liquidity sweep transitions the range, which is the faithful reading. On: price trading through a boundary also transitions it, which stops a stale boundary being drawn through price when no pool sits there.")
boxOn   = input.bool(true, "Premium / discount box", group = gRange, tooltip = "Drawn over the primary range and split at 0.5 only: 1 at the high, 0 at the low. Its midline replaces the EQ stroke; the EQ label and its odds stay. PREMIUM and DISCOUNT text takes each half's colour at full strength.")
colPrem = input.color(color.new(#787B86, 88), "Premium", inline = "bx", group = gRange)
colDisc = input.color(color.new(#C9A227, 90), "Discount", inline = "bx", group = gRange)
colMid  = input.color(#E0A800, "Midline", inline = "bx", group = gRange)

gRef = "6. Delivery range"
dlvOn  = input.bool(false, "Delivery range", inline = "rf", group = gRef)
colRef = input.color(#FF9800, "", inline = "rf", group = gRef)
widRef = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "rf", group = gRef, tooltip = "A registered purge arms it; a confirmed CLOSE through the last opposing chart-TF swing forms it - close, not wick, so the next stop run cannot pass as displacement. It runs from the raid extreme to the displacement extreme, which keeps extending with price. It ends when price takes the raid extreme back, or when a newer raid and close through structure forms. No ATR threshold, no ranking, no FVG requirement.")

gDraw = "7. Draw"
showDraw = input.bool(true, "Mark the draw", inline = "dw", group = gDraw)
colDraw  = input.color(#FFEB3B, "", inline = "dw", group = gDraw)

gOdds = "8. Odds"
oddsOn    = input.bool(true, "Show odds", group = gOdds, tooltip = "Prices every live level as p = 1/(1+k), where k is its distance in R. That is the first-passage probability of reaching the level before a 1R stop for a driftless process - the no-edge baseline. It is not a forecast and not a signal. Whatever edge your read has is the amount by which it must beat this number.")
oddsRisk  = input.string("ATR multiple", "Risk from", options = ["ATR multiple", "Manual points", "Distance to last swing"], group = gOdds, tooltip = "The denominator. It must not be the dealing range itself - risk measured to the opposite boundary makes the odds column print your position in the range and nothing else. Last swing uses the register's own swing length and is side-aware: a level above price is priced against the drop to the last swing low, a level below it against the rise to the last swing high.")
oddsAtrX  = input.float(1.5, "…ATR multiple", minval = 0.1, maxval = 20, step = 0.1, group = gOdds)
oddsManPt = input.float(0, "…Manual points", minval = 0, group = gOdds)
oddsCost  = input.float(1.5, "Round-trip cost (points)", minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = gOdds, tooltip = "Commission plus expected slippage, both ways, in points. Above zero a second figure appears: the win rate needed after cost, which is the baseline times (1 + cost/R). Net expectancy on this model is minus the cost in R at every distance, so the stop in points is the only lever that moves it.")
oddsCapR  = input.float(6, "Price levels out to (R)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 50, step = 0.5, group = gOdds, tooltip = "Levels beyond this are left unpriced. The cap sets the floor odds you will ever see printed: 6R is 14%, 8R is 11%, 4R is 20%.")
oddsAll   = input.bool(true, "Price register levels", group = gOdds, tooltip = "Off prices only the range boundaries, EQ and the draw.")
oddsDim   = input.bool(true, "Dim below one-in-three", inline = "od", group = gOdds, tooltip = "Fades register levels beyond 2R, where distance alone has already decided them. The figure is ADDED to the level colour's own transparency, so with the register at 50% a fade of 25 lands at 75%. Keep the sum under about 85 or faded levels disappear rather than recede.")
oddsFade  = input.int(25, "", minval = 0, maxval = 90, inline = "od", group = gOdds)

gVc = "9. Volume context"
vcOn       = input.bool(false, "Enable volume context", group = gVc, tooltip = "A volume profile, point of control and value area anchored to the live dealing range. Nothing is computed or drawn until a range exists, and the whole thing recomputes when the range reframes. Not an ICT construct - treat it as context, not a signal.")
vcPocShow  = input.bool(true, "POC line", inline = "vp", group = gVc, tooltip = "The single highest-volume row in the range. Drawn from the older of the two boundary anchors and extended right with the range lines.")
vcPocCol   = input.color(#E8A33D, "", inline = "vp", group = gVc)
vcPocWid   = input.int(2, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "vp", group = gVc)
vcVaShow   = input.bool(true, "Value area", inline = "va", group = gVc, tooltip = "VAH and VAL: the band around the POC that holds this share of the volume traded inside the range, built by adding the heavier neighbouring row, above or below, until the share is reached. Inside it the market accepted price; beyond it trade thinned out. Seventy is the classical figure.")
vcVaCol    = input.color(color.new(#E8A33D, 40), "", inline = "va", group = gVc)
vcVaPct    = input.int(70, "%", minval = 50, maxval = 95, inline = "va", group = gVc)
vcFpOn     = input.bool(false, "Real volume at price", inline = "fp", group = gVc, tooltip = "Needs TradingView Premium or Ultimate. On: each candle's volume is placed at the prices it actually traded, from TradingView's footprint data, instead of being spread evenly across the candle's high to low. On a lower plan the script stops with an error while this is on - switch it off. Candles with no footprint data, such as history beyond what the plan provides, fall back to the even spread; the POC label's tooltip says how many candles used real data. Ticks per row sets the footprint's own row size: smaller is finer and slower.")
vcFpTicks  = input.int(4, "ticks per row", minval = 1, maxval = 100, inline = "fp", group = gVc)
vcProfShow  = input.bool(false, "Volume profile", inline = "vf", group = gVc, tooltip = "The full histogram. It is anchored outside the primary range / premium-discount box instead of against the last candle. Off by default - the POC line carries most of the information.")
vcProfCol   = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "", inline = "vf", group = gVc)
vcProfFill  = input.int(88, "", minval = 0, maxval = 100, inline = "vf", group = gVc)
vcProfGap   = input.int(8, "Profile gap (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, inline = "vg", group = gVc, tooltip = "Empty space between the right edge of the primary range / premium-discount box and the nearest edge of the widest volume-profile row.")
vcProfWidth = input.int(32, "Profile width (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 150, inline = "vg", group = gVc, tooltip = "Maximum histogram width. This changes the profile width without changing its gap from the range box.")
vcAtrLen   = input.int(100, "ATR length", minval = 5, maxval = 500, inline = "vb", group = gVc)
vcBinMult  = input.float(0.2, "x", minval = 0.02, maxval = 2.0, step = 0.02, inline = "vb", group = gVc, tooltip = "Row height is ATR times this multiplier, so rows scale to volatility rather than to a fixed tick count. Lower is finer and costs more to compute.")
vcMaxRows  = input.int(150, "Max rows", minval = 10, maxval = 400, group = gVc, tooltip = "Caps the row count on very tall ranges. When the cap bites, row height is recomputed so the rows still tile the range exactly.")
vcMaxLook  = input.int(1000, "Max lookback (bars)", minval = 50, maxval = 1900, group = gVc, tooltip = "Safety cap. If the range anchor is older than this, the profile starts here instead of at the anchor.")

gTbl = "10. Table"
tblOn     = input.bool(false, "Show table", group = gTbl)
tblPos    = input.string("Top right", "Position", options = ["Top right", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Middle right"], group = gTbl)
tblSize   = input.string("Normal", "Text size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = gTbl)
tblTxt    = input.color(color.new(#424351, 50), "Text", inline = "tb", group = gTbl)
tblBg     = input.color(#F4F4F7, "Background", inline = "tb", group = gTbl)
tblBorder = input.color(#F4F4F7, "Border", inline = "tb", group = gTbl)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// State
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

const int MAX_SWEPT  = 200
const int MAX_SCAN   = 500
const int WICK_CACHE = 24

var array<Level> live = array.new<Level>()
var array<Level> done = array.new<Level>()

var array<Sess> ses = array.from(Sess.new(na, na, na, na), Sess.new(na, na, na, na), Sess.new(na, na, na, na))

// 5 MTF slots plus one for the daily bar used by PDH/PDL
var array<Track> tr = array.from(
     Track.new(na, na, na, na, na, array.new_int(), array.new_int(), array.new_int()),
     Track.new(na, na, na, na, na, array.new_int(), array.new_int(), array.new_int()),
     Track.new(na, na, na, na, na, array.new_int(), array.new_int(), array.new_int()),
     Track.new(na, na, na, na, na, array.new_int(), array.new_int(), array.new_int()),
     Track.new(na, na, na, na, na, array.new_int(), array.new_int(), array.new_int()),
     Track.new(na, na, na, na, na, array.new_int(), array.new_int(), array.new_int()))

var array<string> sNames = array.from(s1Name, s2Name, s3Name)
var array<color>  sCols  = array.from(s1Col, s2Col, s3Col)
var array<string> baseTf = array.from(src1Tf, src2Tf, src3Tf, src4Tf, src5Tf)
var array<bool>   baseOn = array.from(src1On, src2On, src3On, src4On, src5On)

var array<string> useTf  = array.new_string(5, "")
var array<bool>   useSrc = array.new_bool(5, false)

var bool poolHi = false
var bool poolLo = false
var string poolHiTag = ""
var string poolLoTag = ""
var float sweptHiMax = na   // highest buy-side pool swept on this bar
var float sweptLoMin = na   // lowest sell-side pool swept on this bar
var float drawPrev = na     // the draw pool coming into this bar
var int   drawPrevSide = 0  // 1 buy-side, -1 sell-side
bool      drawSwept = false // that exact pool was swept on this bar

// the volume profile reads high/low/volume back to the range anchor,
// which is deeper than the register's wick scan needs
const int VC_BUF = 2000

max_bars_back(time, MAX_SCAN)
max_bars_back(high, VC_BUF)
max_bars_back(low, VC_BUF)
max_bars_back(volume, VC_BUF)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CME clock
//
// CME futures only print while CME trades, so they need nothing here. 24/7
// perps that mirror a CME market are held to the CME calendar: nothing counts
// from Friday 17:00 NY to Sunday 18:00 NY, or in the daily 17:00-18:00 halt.
// The list is explicit on purpose: a true crypto perp has no CME session to
// mirror and must not be clocked. Same list as Dealing Range Liquidity
// Reversal.
//   HIP3XYZ:*            every trade.xyz market (XYZ100, SP500, GOLD, ...)
//   BINANCE:CLUSDT.P     Binance crude oil perp
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

bool isClPerp   = (syminfo.prefix == "BINANCE" and syminfo.ticker == "CLUSDT.P") or str.contains(syminfo.tickerid, "BINANCE:CLUSDT.P")
bool onCmeClock = cmeClockOn and timeframe.isintraday and (syminfo.prefix == "HIP3XYZ" or str.contains(syminfo.ticker, "XYZ100") or isClPerp)

// true while CME is shut at time t
f_cmeShut(int t) =>
    int dw = dayofweek(t, "America/New_York")
    int hm = hour(t, "America/New_York") * 60 + minute(t, "America/New_York")
    dw == dayofweek.saturday or (dw == dayofweek.sunday and hm < 1080) or (dw == dayofweek.friday and hm >= 1020) or (hm >= 1020 and hm < 1080)

bool cmeOpen = not onCmeClock or not f_cmeShut(time)

// the CME day runs 18:00 to 17:00 New York; key it by the date six hours on
int cmeKey = year(time + 21600000, "America/New_York") * 10000 + month(time + 21600000, "America/New_York") * 100 + dayofmonth(time + 21600000, "America/New_York")
var int cmeLastKey = na
bool cmeNewDay = cmeOpen and (na(cmeLastKey) or cmeKey != cmeLastKey)
if barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen
    cmeLastKey := cmeKey

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Helpers
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

f_size(string s) =>
    switch s
        "Tiny"   => size.tiny
        "Small"  => size.small
        "Normal" => size.normal
        "Large"  => size.large
        => size.small

f_tsize(string s) =>
    switch s
        "Tiny"   => size.tiny
        "Small"  => size.small
        "Normal" => size.normal
        "Large"  => size.large
        => size.normal

f_pos(string s) =>
    switch s
        "Top right"    => position.top_right
        "Top left"     => position.top_left
        "Bottom right" => position.bottom_right
        "Bottom left"  => position.bottom_left
        "Middle right" => position.middle_right
        => position.top_right

f_lnStyle() =>
    switch regStyle
        "Dashed" => line.style_dashed
        "Dotted" => line.style_dotted
        => line.style_solid

fmt_tick(float p) =>
    na(p) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(p), format.mintick)

f_label(string name, float p) =>
    showPrice and not na(p) ? name + " " + fmt_tick(p) : name

tfSec(string tf) => timeframe.in_seconds(tf)

hasTag(string tags, string tag) => str.contains("|" + tags + "|", "|" + tag + "|")

addTag(string tags, string tag) =>
    hasTag(tags, tag) ? tags : str.length(tags) == 0 ? tag : tags + "|" + tag

delTag(string tags, string tag) =>
    s = str.replace_all("|" + tags + "|", "|" + tag + "|", "|")
    str.length(s) <= 2 ? "" : str.substring(s, 1, str.length(s) - 1)

tagText(string tags) => str.replace_all(tags, "|", ",")

tfText(string tf) =>
    string outp = tf
    n = str.tonumber(tf)
    if tf == "M" or tf == "1M"
        outp := "1M"
    else if tf == "W" or tf == "1W"
        outp := "1W"
    else if tf == "D" or tf == "1D"
        outp := "1D"
    else if not na(n)
        m = int(n)
        if m < 60
            outp := str.tostring(m) + "m"
        else if m < 1440 and m % 60 == 0
            outp := str.tostring(int(m / 60)) + "h"
        else if m >= 1440 and m % 1440 == 0
            outp := str.tostring(int(m / 1440)) + "D"
        else
            outp := str.tostring(m) + "m"
    outp

hasTf(array<string> a, string tf) =>
    bool hit = false
    if a.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to a.size() - 1
            if not hit and tfSec(a.get(i)) == tfSec(tf)
                hit := true
    hit

// No promotion. A source at or above the chart TF is used as given.
// A source finer than the chart is unusable and is skipped.
resolveSources() =>
    used = array.new_string()
    cs = timeframe.in_seconds()
    for i = 0 to 4
        tf = baseTf.get(i)
        ok = baseOn.get(i) and tfSec(tf) >= cs and not hasTf(used, tf)
        useSrc.set(i, ok)
        if ok
            used.push(tf)
            useTf.set(i, tf)
        else
            useTf.set(i, timeframe.period)
    0

// ── wick cache ───────────────────────────────────────────────

method archive(Track x) =>
    if not na(x.op)
        x.ops.unshift(x.op)
        x.hxs.unshift(x.hx)
        x.lxs.unshift(x.lx)
        if x.ops.size() > WICK_CACHE
            o1 = x.ops.pop()
            o2 = x.hxs.pop()
            o3 = x.lxs.pop()
    0

method trackWick(Track x, int op) =>
    if not na(op)
        if na(x.op)
            x.op := op
            x.h  := high
            x.l  := low
            x.hx := time
            x.lx := time
        else if op != x.op
            x.archive()
            x.op := op
            x.h  := high
            x.l  := low
            x.hx := time
            x.lx := time
        else
            if high >= x.h
                x.h  := high
                x.hx := time
            if low <= x.l
                x.l  := low
                x.lx := time
    0

method wick(Track x, int op, bool hi) =>
    int outp = na
    if not na(op) and x.ops.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to x.ops.size() - 1
            if na(outp) and x.ops.get(i) == op
                outp := hi ? x.hxs.get(i) : x.lxs.get(i)
    outp

anchorSlow(float p, bool hi, int op, int cl) =>
    int outp = op
    if not na(p) and not na(op) and not na(cl)
        lim = math.min(bar_index, MAX_SCAN - 1)
        int i = 0
        bool stop = false
        while i <= lim and not stop
            bt = time[i]
            if bt < op
                stop := true
            else if bt >= op and bt < cl
                bp = hi ? high[i] : low[i]
                if math.abs(bp - p) <= syminfo.mintick * 0.5
                    outp := bt
                    stop := true
            if not stop
                i += 1
    outp

anchor(int id, float p, bool hi, int op, int cl, string tf) =>
    int outp = na
    if tfSec(tf) > timeframe.in_seconds()
        outp := tr.get(id).wick(op, hi)
    else
        outp := op          // source equals the chart TF: the pivot bar is the chart bar
    na(outp) ? anchorSlow(p, hi, op, cl) : outp

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Levels
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

barMs  = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) * 1000
tol    = syminfo.mintick * mergeTicks
xRight = time + barMs * extendBars
atrVal = ta.atr(14)
visLim = maxDistAtr > 0 ? maxDistAtr * nz(atrVal, 0) : float(na)

// ── odds ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// p = 1/(1+k) is the probability of touching a target k·R away
// before a 1R stop, for a process with no drift. It follows from
// optional stopping: p·b - (1-p)·a = 0, so p = a/(a+b), and the
// R's cancel. Gross expectancy is identically zero at every k.
// With a cost c expressed in R, net expectancy is -c at every k
// and the break-even win rate is p·(1+c). Nothing below forecasts
// anything; the denominator is the only term that can be improved.

riskFlat = oddsRisk == "Manual points" ? oddsManPt : nz(atrVal, 0) * oddsAtrX

var float oSwHi = na
var float oSwLo = na
oPh = ta.pivothigh(high, mtfLen, mtfLen)
oPl = ta.pivotlow(low,  mtfLen, mtfLen)
if not na(oPh) and cmeOpen[mtfLen]
    oSwHi := oPh
if not na(oPl) and cmeOpen[mtfLen]
    oSwLo := oPl

// side-aware structural risk, with a fall back to the flat figure
riskUp = not na(oSwLo) and close - oSwLo > 0 ? close - oSwLo : riskFlat
riskDn = not na(oSwHi) and oSwHi - close > 0 ? oSwHi - close : riskFlat

f_risk(bool above) =>
    r = oddsRisk == "Distance to last swing" ? (above ? riskUp : riskDn) : riskFlat
    na(r) or r <= 0 ? float(na) : r

f_k(float lvl) =>
    r = f_risk(lvl > close)
    na(r) or na(lvl) ? float(na) : math.abs(lvl - close) / r

f_p(float k) => na(k) ? float(na) : 1.0 / (1.0 + k)

pctTxt(float p) => na(p) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(p * 100)) + "%"

oddsLbl(float lvl) =>
    string outp = ""
    if oddsOn and not na(lvl)
        k = f_k(lvl)
        if not na(k) and k <= oddsCapR
            p = f_p(k)
            r = f_risk(lvl > close)
            outp := str.tostring(k, "#.#") + "R · " + pctTxt(p)
            if oddsCost > 0 and not na(r)
                outp := outp + " (need " + pctTxt(math.min(1.0, p * (1.0 + oddsCost / r))) + ")"
    outp

f_label2(string name, float p) =>
    base = f_label(name, p)
    od = oddsLbl(p)
    str.length(od) > 0 ? base + "  " + od : base

lvlColor(Level x) =>
    color c = x.swept ? colSwept : colMtf
    if not x.swept
        for i = 0 to sNames.size() - 1
            if hasTag(x.tags, sNames.get(i))
                c := sCols.get(i)
        if hasTag(x.tags, "PDH") or hasTag(x.tags, "PDL")
            c := pdCol
        if oddsOn and oddsAll and oddsDim
            pk = f_p(f_k(x.p))
            if not na(pk) and pk < 1.0 / 3.0
                c := color.new(c, math.min(100, color.t(c) + oddsFade))
    c

markText(Level x) =>
    tg = showOrigin ? tagText(x.tags) : ""
    od = oddsAll and not x.swept ? oddsLbl(x.p) : ""
    if str.length(od) > 0
        tg := str.length(tg) > 0 ? tg + "  " + od : od
    mk = showMarker ? "◎" : ""
    both = str.length(tg) > 0 and str.length(mk) > 0
    x.hi ? (both ? tg + "\n" + mk : tg + mk) : (both ? mk + "\n" + tg : tg + mk)

lblStyle(bool hi) => hi ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up

method restyle(Level x) =>
    c = lvlColor(x)
    if not na(x.ln)
        line.set_color(x.ln, c)
        line.set_width(x.ln, regWidth)
        line.set_style(x.ln, x.swept ? line.style_dotted : f_lnStyle())
    if not na(x.lb)
        label.set_text(x.lb, markText(x))
        label.set_textcolor(x.lb, c)
    if not na(x.tx)
        label.set_text(x.tx, tagText(x.tags))
        label.set_textcolor(x.tx, c)
    0

method advance(Level x, int xr, float lim) =>
    if not x.swept
        bool vis = na(lim) or math.abs(x.p - close) <= lim
        hidden = color.new(color.black, 100)
        if not na(x.ln)
            line.set_x2(x.ln, xr)
            line.set_color(x.ln, vis ? lvlColor(x) : hidden)
        if not na(x.lb)
            label.set_textcolor(x.lb, vis ? lvlColor(x) : hidden)
            // odds move with price, so the text is rewritten per bar
            if oddsOn and oddsAll
                label.set_text(x.lb, markText(x))
    0

method kill(Level x) =>
    if not na(x.ln)
        line.delete(x.ln)
    if not na(x.lb)
        label.delete(x.lb)
    if not na(x.tx)
        label.delete(x.tx)
    0

removeLive(int id) =>
    x = live.get(id)
    x.kill()
    r = live.remove(id)
    0

removeDone(int id) =>
    x = done.get(id)
    x.kill()
    r = done.remove(id)
    0

removeTagAt(int id, string tag) =>
    x = live.get(id)
    x.tags := delTag(x.tags, tag)
    if str.length(x.tags) == 0
        removeLive(id)
    else
        live.set(id, x)
        x.restyle()
    0

clearTag(string tag) =>
    int i = live.size() - 1
    while i >= 0
        x = live.get(i)
        if hasTag(x.tags, tag)
            removeTagAt(i, tag)
        i -= 1
    0

clearAll() =>
    while live.size() > 0
        removeLive(live.size() - 1)
    while done.size() > 0
        removeDone(done.size() - 1)
    0

pruneDone() =>
    while done.size() > MAX_SWEPT
        removeDone(0)
    0

hideOldSweeps() =>
    n = done.size()
    if n > historyN
        for i = 0 to n - historyN - 1
            x = done.get(i)
            if not na(x.ln)
                line.delete(x.ln)
                x.ln := na
            if not na(x.tx)
                label.delete(x.tx)
                x.tx := na
            done.set(i, x)
    0

markSwept(Level x, int st) =>
    x.swept := true
    x.sx := st
    if not na(x.lb)
        label.delete(x.lb)
        x.lb := na
    if not na(x.ln)
        line.set_x2(x.ln, st)
    if showHistory and showRegister and showOrigin
        mid = x.x + int((st - x.x) / 2)
        x.tx := label.new(mid, x.p, tagText(x.tags), xloc = xloc.bar_time, yloc = yloc.price, style = lblStyle(x.hi), color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = colSwept, size = f_size(lblSize), textalign = text.align_center)
    else if not showHistory
        if not na(x.ln)
            line.delete(x.ln)
            x.ln := na
    x.restyle()
    0

addLevel(float raw, bool hi, int ox, string tag) =>
    if not na(raw) and not na(ox) and str.length(tag) > 0
        p = math.round_to_mintick(raw)
        int id = -1
        int i = 0
        while i < live.size() and id == -1
            x = live.get(i)
            if x.hi == hi and math.abs(x.p - p) <= tol
                id := i
            i += 1

        if id >= 0
            x = live.get(id)
            x.tags := addTag(x.tags, tag)
            if ox < x.x
                x.x := ox
                if not na(x.ln)
                    line.set_x1(x.ln, ox)
                if not na(x.lb)
                    label.set_x(x.lb, ox)
            live.set(id, x)
            x.restyle()
        else
            nx = Level.new(p, hi, ox, bar_index, tag, false, na, na, na, na)
            c  = lvlColor(nx)
            if showRegister
                nx.ln := line.new(ox, p, xRight, p, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c, width = regWidth, style = f_lnStyle())
                if showOrigin or showMarker
                    nx.lb := label.new(ox, p, markText(nx), xloc = xloc.bar_time, yloc = yloc.price, style = lblStyle(nx.hi), color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = c, size = f_size(lblSize), textalign = text.align_center)
            live.push(nx)
    0

countTag(string tag, bool hi) =>
    int n = 0
    if live.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to live.size() - 1
            x = live.get(i)
            if x.hi == hi and hasTag(x.tags, tag)
                n += 1
    n

trim(string tag, bool hi, int keep) =>
    int n = countTag(tag, hi)
    while n > keep
        int id = -1
        int oldest = na
        if live.size() > 0
            for i = 0 to live.size() - 1
                x = live.get(i)
                if x.hi == hi and hasTag(x.tags, tag)
                    if id == -1 or x.x < oldest
                        id := i
                        oldest := x.x
        if id >= 0
            removeTagAt(id, tag)
            n -= 1
        else
            n := keep
    0

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Sources
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

if barstate.isfirst
    resolveSources()

pivots(int len) =>
    ph = ta.pivothigh(high, len, len)
    pl = ta.pivotlow(low, len, len)
    [ph, na(ph) ? int(na) : time[len], na(ph) ? int(na) : time_close[len], pl, na(pl) ? int(na) : time[len], na(pl) ? int(na) : time_close[len]]

[ph1, pht1, phc1, pl1, plt1, plc1] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, useTf.get(0), pivots(mtfLen), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[ph2, pht2, phc2, pl2, plt2, plc2] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, useTf.get(1), pivots(mtfLen), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[ph3, pht3, phc3, pl3, plt3, plc3] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, useTf.get(2), pivots(mtfLen), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[ph4, pht4, phc4, pl4, plt4, plc4] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, useTf.get(3), pivots(mtfLen), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[ph5, pht5, phc5, pl5, plt5, plc5] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, useTf.get(4), pivots(mtfLen), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

pdh   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", high[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
pdl   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", low[1],  lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
pdOpn = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", time[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
pdCls = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", time_close[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

cs = timeframe.in_seconds()
if barstate.isconfirmed
    if useSrc.get(0) and tfSec(useTf.get(0)) > cs
        tr.get(0).trackWick(time(useTf.get(0)))
    if useSrc.get(1) and tfSec(useTf.get(1)) > cs
        tr.get(1).trackWick(time(useTf.get(1)))
    if useSrc.get(2) and tfSec(useTf.get(2)) > cs
        tr.get(2).trackWick(time(useTf.get(2)))
    if useSrc.get(3) and tfSec(useTf.get(3)) > cs
        tr.get(3).trackWick(time(useTf.get(3)))
    if useSrc.get(4) and tfSec(useTf.get(4)) > cs
        tr.get(4).trackWick(time(useTf.get(4)))
    if pdOn and tfSec("D") > cs
        tr.get(5).trackWick(time("D"))

processPivot(int id, bool on, float ph, int pht, int phc, float pl, int plt, int plc, string tag, string tf) =>
    if on and barstate.isconfirmed
        newHi = not na(pht) and (na(pht[1]) or pht != pht[1])
        newLo = not na(plt) and (na(plt[1]) or plt != plt[1])
        // a swing printed while CME was shut is not on the futures chart
        if onCmeClock and newHi and f_cmeShut(pht)
            newHi := false
        if onCmeClock and newLo and f_cmeShut(plt)
            newLo := false
        if newHi
            hx = anchor(id, ph, true, pht, phc, tf)
            addLevel(ph, true, hx, tag)
            trim(tag, true, levelsN)
        if newLo
            lx = anchor(id, pl, false, plt, plc, tf)
            addLevel(pl, false, lx, tag)
            trim(tag, false, levelsN)
    0

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Day roll and sessions
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

TZ = "America/New_York"
symNewDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
newDay = onCmeClock ? cmeNewDay : symNewDay

// on the CME clock, PDH / PDL are the previous CME day's extremes, read
// from the candles CME printed, anchored at the candle that made them
var float cdHi  = na
var float cdLo  = na
var int   cdHiT = na
var int   cdLoT = na
var float cpHi  = na
var float cpLo  = na
var int   cpHiT = na
var int   cpLoT = na
if barstate.isconfirmed and onCmeClock and cmeOpen
    if newDay
        cpHi  := cdHi
        cpLo  := cdLo
        cpHiT := cdHiT
        cpLoT := cdLoT
        cdHi  := high
        cdLo  := low
        cdHiT := time
        cdLoT := time
    else
        if na(cdHi) or high > cdHi
            cdHi  := high
            cdHiT := time
        if na(cdLo) or low < cdLo
            cdLo  := low
            cdLoT := time

if barstate.isconfirmed and newDay and not barstate.isfirst
    if dailyReset
        clearAll()
    else
        for i = 0 to sNames.size() - 1
            clearTag(sNames.get(i))
        clearTag("PDH")
        clearTag("PDL")
    if pdOn and onCmeClock
        if not na(cpHi)
            addLevel(cpHi, true, cpHiT, "PDH")
            addLevel(cpLo, false, cpLoT, "PDL")
    else if pdOn and not na(pdh)
        hx = anchor(5, pdh, true, pdOpn, pdCls, "D")
        lx = anchor(5, pdl, false, pdOpn, pdCls, "D")
        addLevel(pdh, true, hx, "PDH")
        addLevel(pdl, false, lx, "PDL")

method runSession(Sess s, bool inside, bool st, bool ed, string tag) =>
    if st
        s.h := high
        s.l := low
        s.hx := time
        s.lx := time
    else if inside
        if na(s.h) or high > s.h
            s.h := high
            s.hx := time
        if na(s.l) or low < s.l
            s.l := low
            s.lx := time
    if ed and not na(s.h)
        addLevel(s.h, true, s.hx, tag)
        addLevel(s.l, false, s.lx, tag)
        trim(tag, true, levelsN)
        trim(tag, false, levelsN)
        s.h := na
        s.l := na
        s.hx := na
        s.lx := na
    0

in1 = s1On and not na(time(timeframe.period, s1Time, TZ)) and cmeOpen
in2 = s2On and not na(time(timeframe.period, s2Time, TZ)) and cmeOpen
in3 = s3On and not na(time(timeframe.period, s3Time, TZ)) and cmeOpen

if barstate.isconfirmed
    ses.get(0).runSession(in1, in1 and not in1[1], not in1 and in1[1], sNames.get(0))
    ses.get(1).runSession(in2, in2 and not in2[1], not in2 and in2[1], sNames.get(1))
    ses.get(2).runSession(in3, in3 and not in3[1], not in3 and in3[1], sNames.get(2))

processPivot(0, useSrc.get(0), ph1, pht1, phc1, pl1, plt1, plc1, tfText(useTf.get(0)), useTf.get(0))
processPivot(1, useSrc.get(1), ph2, pht2, phc2, pl2, plt2, plc2, tfText(useTf.get(1)), useTf.get(1))
processPivot(2, useSrc.get(2), ph3, pht3, phc3, pl3, plt3, plc3, tfText(useTf.get(2)), useTf.get(2))
processPivot(3, useSrc.get(3), ph4, pht4, phc4, pl4, plt4, plc4, tfText(useTf.get(3)), useTf.get(3))
processPivot(4, useSrc.get(4), ph5, pht5, phc5, pl5, plt5, plc5, tfText(useTf.get(4)), useTf.get(4))

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Sweep
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

poolHi := false
poolLo := false
poolHiTag := ""
poolLoTag := ""
sweptHiMax := na
sweptLoMin := na

if barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen
    int i = 0
    while i < live.size()
        x = live.get(i)
        x.advance(xRight, visLim)
        bool hit = time > x.x and (x.hi ? high >= x.p : low <= x.p)
        if hit
            markSwept(x, time)
            r = live.remove(i)
            done.push(x)
            hideOldSweeps()
            if x.hi
                poolHi := true
                if drawPrevSide == 1 and not na(drawPrev) and math.abs(x.p - drawPrev) <= syminfo.mintick * 0.5
                    drawSwept := true
                sweptHiMax := na(sweptHiMax) ? x.p : math.max(sweptHiMax, x.p)
                if str.length(poolHiTag) == 0
                    poolHiTag := tagText(x.tags)
            else
                poolLo := true
                if drawPrevSide == -1 and not na(drawPrev) and math.abs(x.p - drawPrev) <= syminfo.mintick * 0.5
                    drawSwept := true
                sweptLoMin := na(sweptLoMin) ? x.p : math.min(sweptLoMin, x.p)
                if str.length(poolLoTag) == 0
                    poolLoTag := tagText(x.tags)
            pruneDone()
        else
            i += 1
else if barstate.islast
    if live.size() > 0
        for k = 0 to live.size() - 1
            live.get(k).advance(xRight, visLim)

// every registered sweep reaches the range engines
passHi = poolHi
passLo = poolLo

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Dealing range
//
// No range until liquidity frames one. A registered purge opens the
// matching side; the opposing purge completes the pair. The tracking
// side following its excursion is development, not a reframe.
//
// Rotation - any opposing purge re-anchors that side at the purging bar.
// Frame    - identical until both sides are set. After that only a purge
//            of a pool at or beyond a boundary moves it, and the moved
//            side can only widen.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

method update(Rng r, bool tookHi, bool tookLo, bool widen) =>
    r.reframed := false
    r.extended := false
    r.contracted := false
    if tookHi and tookLo
        // Both sides taken on one bar. OHLC cannot establish the order, so
        // only what holds in EITHER order is applied: a side that was not
        // being tracked re-anchors to this bar, and the side that was being
        // tracked can only extend - re-anchoring it would assume its sweep
        // came last. Direction is unknown, so tracking and the draw are
        // suspended until the next single-sided purge.
        r.amb := true
        int prev = r.st
        if prev != 1
            if not (widen and r.hiSet and r.hi > high)
                r.hi  := high
                r.hiT := time
                r.hiB := bar_index
            r.reframed := r.hiSet
            r.hiSet := true
        else if high > r.hi
            r.hi  := high
            r.hiT := time
            r.hiB := bar_index
            r.extended := true
        if prev != -1
            if not (widen and r.loSet and r.lo < low)
                r.lo  := low
                r.loT := time
                r.loB := bar_index
            r.reframed := r.reframed or r.loSet
            r.loSet := true
        else if low < r.lo
            r.lo  := low
            r.loT := time
            r.loB := bar_index
            r.extended := true
        r.st := 0
    else if tookHi
        r.amb := false
        if r.st != 1
            r.reframed := true
            r.st := 1
            if not (widen and r.hiSet and r.hi > high)
                r.hi  := high
                r.hiT := time
                r.hiB := bar_index
            r.hiSet := true
    else if tookLo
        r.amb := false
        if r.st != -1
            r.reframed := true
            r.st := -1
            if not (widen and r.loSet and r.lo < low)
                r.lo  := low
                r.loT := time
                r.loB := bar_index
            r.loSet := true
    if r.st == 1 and r.hiSet and high > r.hi
        r.hi  := high
        r.hiT := time
        r.hiB := bar_index
        r.extended := true
    if r.st == -1 and r.loSet and low < r.lo
        r.lo  := low
        r.loT := time
        r.loB := bar_index
        r.extended := true
    0

method isLive(Rng r) => r.hiSet and r.loSet and not na(r.hi) and not na(r.lo) and r.hi > r.lo

// Delivery. A raid arms it in the opposite direction and records the last
// confirmed chart-TF swing on the other side. A confirmed close through that
// swing forms it. A newer raid on either side re-arms; a double raid on one
// bar disarms, since the order cannot be known.
method step(Dlv d, bool rHi, bool rLo, float swLo, float swHi) =>
    d.formed := false
    d.extended := false
    // an active delivery ends when its raid extreme is taken back
    if d.dir == -1
        if high >= d.hi
            d.dir := 0
        else if low < d.lo
            d.lo  := low
            d.loT := time
            d.loB := bar_index
            d.extended := true
    else if d.dir == 1
        if low <= d.lo
            d.dir := 0
        else if high > d.hi
            d.hi  := high
            d.hiT := time
            d.hiB := bar_index
            d.extended := true

    if rHi and rLo
        d.pend := 0
    else if rHi
        d.pend  := -1
        d.pExt  := high
        d.pExtT := time
        d.pExtB := bar_index
        d.pOpp  := low
        d.pOppT := time
        d.pOppB := bar_index
        d.pMss  := swLo
    else if rLo
        d.pend  := 1
        d.pExt  := low
        d.pExtT := time
        d.pExtB := bar_index
        d.pOpp  := high
        d.pOppT := time
        d.pOppB := bar_index
        d.pMss  := swHi
    else if d.pend == -1
        if high > d.pExt
            d.pExt  := high
            d.pExtT := time
            d.pExtB := bar_index
        if low < d.pOpp
            d.pOpp  := low
            d.pOppT := time
            d.pOppB := bar_index
    else if d.pend == 1
        if low < d.pExt
            d.pExt  := low
            d.pExtT := time
            d.pExtB := bar_index
        if high > d.pOpp
            d.pOpp  := high
            d.pOppT := time
            d.pOppB := bar_index

    if d.pend == -1 and not na(d.pMss) and close < d.pMss
        d.dir := -1
        d.hi  := d.pExt
        d.hiT := d.pExtT
        d.hiB := d.pExtB
        d.lo  := d.pOpp
        d.loT := d.pOppT
        d.loB := d.pOppB
        d.pend := 0
        d.formed := true
    else if d.pend == 1 and not na(d.pMss) and close > d.pMss
        d.dir := 1
        d.lo  := d.pExt
        d.loT := d.pExtT
        d.loB := d.pExtB
        d.hi  := d.pOpp
        d.hiT := d.pOppT
        d.hiB := d.pOppB
        d.pend := 0
        d.formed := true
    0

// ── IPDA window ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// One record per Daily bar of the symbol, newest first: its high and
// low and the chart bar that printed each. The window is the current
// Daily bar plus the previous lookback-1, so its extremes agree with the
// same count on a Daily chart. Recalculated every day.

var array<int>   ipDayT = array.new<int>()
var array<float> ipHiP  = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   ipHiT  = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   ipHiB  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> ipLoP  = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   ipLoT  = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   ipLoB  = array.new<int>()
var bool         ipPartial = false   // the oldest record began mid-day on the first loaded bar

if barstate.isconfirmed and frameOn and cmeOpen
    if newDay or ipDayT.size() == 0
        if ipDayT.size() == 0 and not newDay
            ipPartial := true
        ipDayT.unshift(time)
        ipHiP.unshift(high)
        ipHiT.unshift(time)
        ipHiB.unshift(bar_index)
        ipLoP.unshift(low)
        ipLoT.unshift(time)
        ipLoB.unshift(bar_index)
        while ipDayT.size() > 60
            ipPartial := false   // the oldest record, the partial one, is the one leaving
            ipDayT.pop()
            ipHiP.pop()
            ipHiT.pop()
            ipHiB.pop()
            ipLoP.pop()
            ipLoT.pop()
            ipLoB.pop()
    else
        if high > ipHiP.get(0)
            ipHiP.set(0, high)
            ipHiT.set(0, time)
            ipHiB.set(0, bar_index)
        if low < ipLoP.get(0)
            ipLoP.set(0, low)
            ipLoT.set(0, time)
            ipLoB.set(0, bar_index)

// full Daily records available; the current Daily bar counts, as it does
// in the same count on a Daily chart
ipDays    = ipDayT.size() - (ipPartial ? 1 : 0)
ipdaReady = ipDays >= ipdaLb

// the extreme on one side across the newest n Daily records
f_ipExt(bool hi, int n) =>
    float p = na
    int   t = na
    int   b = na
    for i = 0 to n - 1
        v = hi ? ipHiP.get(i) : ipLoP.get(i)
        if na(p) or (hi ? v > p : v < p)
            p := v
            t := hi ? ipHiT.get(i) : ipLoT.get(i)
            b := hi ? ipHiB.get(i) : ipLoB.get(i)
    [p, t, b]

var Rng rot = Rng.new()
var Rng frm = Rng.new()
var Dlv dlv = Dlv.new()
var int    lastSweep = 0 // 1 buy-side, -1 sell-side, 2 both on one bar
var string lastSweepTag = ""

if barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen
    if passHi and passLo
        lastSweep := 2
        lastSweepTag := ""
    else if passHi
        lastSweep := 1
        lastSweepTag := poolHiTag
    else if passLo
        lastSweep := -1
        lastSweepTag := poolLoTag

    if rotOn
        rEdgeHi = edgeTrigger and rot.hiSet and rot.st != 1 and high >= rot.hi
        rEdgeLo = edgeTrigger and rot.loSet and rot.st != -1 and low <= rot.lo
        rot.update(passHi or rEdgeHi, passLo or rEdgeLo, false)

    if frameOn
        // once framed, a purge counts only when the swept pool sits at or
        // beyond the boundary - external range liquidity
        framed  = frm.hiSet and frm.loSet
        fExtHi  = passHi and (not framed or sweptHiMax >= frm.hi - tol)
        fExtLo  = passLo and (not framed or sweptLoMin <= frm.lo + tol)
        fEdgeHi = edgeTrigger and frm.hiSet and frm.st != 1 and high >= frm.hi
        fEdgeLo = edgeTrigger and frm.loSet and frm.st != -1 and low <= frm.lo
        frm.update(fExtHi or fEdgeHi, fExtLo or fEdgeLo, true)
        // IPDA contraction: no boundary may be older than the lookback.
        // An aged boundary moves to that side's extreme inside the window.
        // Only once a full window exists; until then the frame stays a pure
        // liquidity frame and is marked not ready.
        if ipdaReady
            n = ipdaLb
            wStart = ipDayT.get(n - 1)
            if frm.hiSet and frm.hiT < wStart
                [hP, hT, hB] = f_ipExt(true, n)
                frm.hi  := hP
                frm.hiT := hT
                frm.hiB := hB
                frm.contracted := true
            if frm.loSet and frm.loT < wStart
                [lP, lT, lB] = f_ipExt(false, n)
                frm.lo  := lP
                frm.loT := lT
                frm.loB := lB
                frm.contracted := true

    if dlvOn
        dlv.step(passHi, passLo, oSwLo, oSwHi)

// ── manual range ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// the extremes from the candle holding manFrom through the candle holding
// manTo, both included, anchored at the candles that printed them. On any
// timeframe the candle a time falls in counts. Nothing moves it after.

var float mHi  = na
var float mLo  = na
var int   mHiT = na
var int   mLoT = na
var int   mHiB = na
var int   mLoB = na
manOn = primSel == "Manual"
if manOn and barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen and time_close > manFrom and time <= manTo
    if na(mHi) or high > mHi
        mHi  := high
        mHiT := time
        mHiB := bar_index
    if na(mLo) or low < mLo
        mLo  := low
        mLoT := time
        mLoB := bar_index
manLive = manOn and not na(mHi) and not na(mLo) and mHi > mLo

// ── primary range ────────────────────────────────────────────
// the box, EQ, position, draw, boundary odds, volume profile, table
// and alerts all measure against this one

rotLive = rotOn and rot.isLive()
frmLive = frameOn and frm.isLive()
dlvLive = dlvOn and dlv.dir != 0 and not na(dlv.hi) and not na(dlv.lo) and dlv.hi > dlv.lo

// the chosen range if it is live, else the first live range, else the
// chosen one if switched on (so the table can show it developing)
reqLive = primSel == "Rotation" ? rotLive : primSel == "IPDA Frame" ? frmLive : primSel == "Delivery" ? dlvLive : manLive
reqOn   = primSel == "Rotation" ? rotOn : primSel == "IPDA Frame" ? frameOn : primSel == "Delivery" ? dlvOn : manOn
prim    = reqLive ? primSel : rotLive ? "Rotation" : frmLive ? "IPDA Frame" : dlvLive ? "Delivery" : reqOn ? primSel : rotOn ? "Rotation" : frameOn ? "IPDA Frame" : dlvOn ? "Delivery" : "None"
frmName  = "IPDA Frame " + str.tostring(ipdaLb) + "D" + (ipdaReady ? "" : " (not ready, " + str.tostring(ipDays) + "D loaded)")
primName = (prim == "IPDA Frame" ? frmName : prim) + (prim != primSel and prim != "None" ? " (fallback)" : "")
isRot = prim == "Rotation"
isFrm = prim == "IPDA Frame"
isDlv = prim == "Delivery"
isMan = prim == "Manual"

cHi  = isRot ? rot.hi  : isFrm ? frm.hi  : isDlv ? dlv.hi  : isMan ? mHi  : float(na)
cLo  = isRot ? rot.lo  : isFrm ? frm.lo  : isDlv ? dlv.lo  : isMan ? mLo  : float(na)
cHiT = isRot ? rot.hiT : isFrm ? frm.hiT : isDlv ? dlv.hiT : isMan ? mHiT : int(na)
cLoT = isRot ? rot.loT : isFrm ? frm.loT : isDlv ? dlv.loT : isMan ? mLoT : int(na)
cHiB = isRot ? rot.hiB : isFrm ? frm.hiB : isDlv ? dlv.hiB : isMan ? mHiB : int(na)
cLoB = isRot ? rot.loB : isFrm ? frm.loB : isDlv ? dlv.loB : isMan ? mLoB : int(na)

// a bearish delivery follows a buy-side raid, so it reads as tracking the high
primSt  = isRot ? rot.st : isFrm ? frm.st : isDlv ? -dlv.dir : 0
primAmb = isRot ? rot.amb : isFrm ? frm.amb : false
primDev = isRot ? (rot.hiSet or rot.loSet) : isFrm ? (frm.hiSet or frm.loSet) : isDlv ? (dlv.pend != 0) : isMan ? not na(mHi) : false

rangeLive = (isRot ? rotLive : isFrm ? frmLive : isDlv ? dlvLive : isMan ? manLive : false) and not na(cHi) and not na(cLo) and cHi > cLo

var bool wasLive = false
firstLive = rangeLive and not wasLive
wasLive := rangeLive

rangeReframed    = barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen and rangeLive and not firstLive and (isRot ? rot.reframed : isFrm ? frm.reframed : isDlv ? dlv.formed : false)
boundaryExtended = barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen and rangeLive and (isRot ? rot.extended : isFrm ? frm.extended : isDlv ? dlv.extended : false)
dlvFormed        = barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen and dlvLive and dlv.formed
frmContracted    = barstate.isconfirmed and cmeOpen and frmLive and frm.contracted

wkEq = rangeLive ? (cHi + cLo) / 2 : float(na)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Draw
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

drawSide = primAmb ? 0 : primSt == 1 ? -1 : primSt == -1 ? 1 : 0

float drawLvl = na
string drawTag = ""

if rangeLive and drawSide != 0 and live.size() > 0
    for k = 0 to live.size() - 1
        x = live.get(k)
        if (x.hi and drawSide == 1 and x.p > close) or (not x.hi and drawSide == -1 and x.p < close)
            if na(drawLvl) or math.abs(x.p - close) < math.abs(drawLvl - close)
                drawLvl := x.p
                drawTag := tagText(x.tags)

drawPrev     := drawLvl
drawPrevSide := na(drawLvl) ? 0 : drawSide

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Dealing range drawing
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

var line  lnHi = na
var line  lnLo = na
var line  lnEq = na
var label lbHi = na
var label lbLo = na
var label lbEq = na
var label lbDr = na
// redrawn on the last bar: the other ranges, the box, its midline and scale
var array<line>  exLines  = array.new<line>()
var array<label> exLabels = array.new<label>()
var array<box>   exBoxes  = array.new<box>()

// a label on the same row as a primary range label drops one row below it
f_lblStyle(float p) =>
    float d = rangeLive ? math.max(tol, 0.015 * (cHi - cLo)) : tol
    bool clash = rangeLive and (math.abs(p - cHi) <= d or math.abs(p - cLo) <= d or (showEq and math.abs(p - wkEq) <= d))
    clash ? label.style_label_upper_left : label.style_label_left

f_other(float h, float l, int hT, int lT, string name, color cH, color cL, int w, string sty, bool mid) =>
    exLines.push(line.new(hT, h, xRight, h, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = cH, width = w, style = sty))
    exLines.push(line.new(lT, l, xRight, l, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = cL, width = w, style = sty))
    exLabels.push(label.new(xRight, h, f_label(name + " HIGH", h), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = f_lblStyle(h), color = color.new(cH, 100), textcolor = cH, size = f_size(lblSize)))
    exLabels.push(label.new(xRight, l, f_label(name + " LOW", l), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = f_lblStyle(l), color = color.new(cL, 100), textcolor = cL, size = f_size(lblSize)))
    if mid
        m = (h + l) / 2
        exLines.push(line.new(math.max(hT, lT), m, xRight, m, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = cH, width = 1, style = line.style_dotted))
    0

if barstate.islast
    line.delete(lnHi)
    line.delete(lnLo)
    line.delete(lnEq)
    label.delete(lbHi)
    label.delete(lbLo)
    label.delete(lbEq)
    label.delete(lbDr)
    lnHi := na
    lnLo := na
    lnEq := na
    lbHi := na
    lbLo := na
    lbEq := na
    lbDr := na
    for ln in exLines
        line.delete(ln)
    exLines.clear()
    for lb in exLabels
        label.delete(lb)
    exLabels.clear()
    for bx in exBoxes
        box.delete(bx)
    exBoxes.clear()

    if rangeLive
        if showHi
            lnHi := line.new(cHiT, cHi, xRight, cHi, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = colHi, width = widHi, style = line.style_solid)
            lbHi := label.new(xRight, cHi, f_label2(txtHi, cHi), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colHi, 100), textcolor = colHi, size = f_size(lblSize))
        if showLo
            lnLo := line.new(cLoT, cLo, xRight, cLo, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = colLo, width = widLo, style = line.style_solid)
            lbLo := label.new(xRight, cLo, f_label2(txtLo, cLo), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colLo, 100), textcolor = colLo, size = f_size(lblSize))
        if showEq
            // with the box on, its gold midline is the EQ stroke; the label stays
            cEq = boxOn ? colMid : colEq
            if not boxOn
                eqStart = math.max(cHiT, cLoT)
                lnEq := line.new(eqStart, wkEq, xRight, wkEq, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = colEq, width = widEq, style = line.style_dashed)
            lbEq := label.new(xRight, wkEq, f_label2(txtEq, wkEq), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(cEq, 100), textcolor = cEq, size = f_size(lblSize))
        // premium / discount box over the primary range, split at 0.5 only
        if boxOn
            bxL   = math.min(cHiT, cLoT)
            cPm   = color.new(colPrem, 0)
            cDs   = color.new(colDisc, 0)
            cNone = color.new(color.black, 100)
            exBoxes.push(box.new(bxL, cHi, xRight, wkEq, xloc = xloc.bar_time, border_color = cNone, border_width = 1, bgcolor = colPrem, text = "PREMIUM", text_color = cPm, text_size = f_size(lblSize), text_halign = text.align_right, text_valign = text.align_top))
            exBoxes.push(box.new(bxL, wkEq, xRight, cLo, xloc = xloc.bar_time, border_color = cNone, border_width = 1, bgcolor = colDisc, text = "DISCOUNT", text_color = cDs, text_size = f_size(lblSize), text_halign = text.align_right, text_valign = text.align_bottom))
            exLines.push(line.new(bxL, wkEq, xRight, wkEq, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = colMid, width = 1, style = line.style_solid))
            exLabels.push(label.new(bxL, cHi,  "1",   xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_right, color = cNone, textcolor = cPm,    size = f_size(lblSize)))
            exLabels.push(label.new(bxL, wkEq, "0.5", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_right, color = cNone, textcolor = colMid, size = f_size(lblSize)))
            exLabels.push(label.new(bxL, cLo,  "0",   xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_right, color = cNone, textcolor = cDs,    size = f_size(lblSize)))
        // no fallback: a range boundary is not automatically an unswept objective
        if showDraw and drawSide != 0 and not na(drawLvl)
            dOdds = oddsLbl(drawLvl)
            dTxt = "DRAW → " + (drawSide == 1 ? "BSL" : "SSL") + (drawTag == "" ? "" : " " + drawTag) + (str.length(dOdds) > 0 ? "  " + dOdds : "")
            lbDr := label.new(xRight, drawLvl, dTxt, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = drawSide == 1 ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left, color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = colDraw, size = f_size(lblSize))

    // the other ranges that are on, drawn quieter than the primary.
    // a range identical to the primary is drawn once.
    if rotLive and not isRot and not (rot.hi == cHi and rot.lo == cLo)
        f_other(rot.hi, rot.lo, rot.hiT, rot.loT, "ROTATION", colHi, colLo, 1, line.style_dotted, false)
    if frmLive and not isFrm and not (frm.hi == cHi and frm.lo == cLo)
        f_other(frm.hi, frm.lo, frm.hiT, frm.loT, str.upper(frmName), colHi, colLo, 1, line.style_dotted, false)
    if dlvLive and not isDlv
        f_other(dlv.hi, dlv.lo, dlv.hiT, dlv.loT, "DELIVERY", colRef, colRef, widRef, line.style_dashed, true)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Volume context - profile and POC anchored to the dealing range
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Rows are sized by ATR, not by a fixed tick count, so the profile
// scales with volatility. Each bar's volume is spread across every
// row its high-low range touches, weighted by overlap against the
// bar's FULL range - so volume traded outside the range boundaries
// is not credited to the rows inside them. The rows therefore sum
// to less than total volume by design: this describes trade within
// the range, which is the only thing the range can speak to.

var float    vcPoc   = na
var float    vcVah   = na
var float    vcVal   = na
var bool     vcValid = false
var polyline vcPoly  = na
var line     vcLine  = na
var label    vcLbl   = na
var line     vcVahLn = na
var line     vcValLn = na
var label    vcVahLb = na
var label    vcValLb = na

vcAtr = ta.atr(vcAtrLen)

// Real volume at price. The request sits behind a real conditional, so
// with the option off it never runs and lower plans never hit the
// footprint plan check.
footprint vcFp = na
if vcOn and vcFpOn
    vcFp := request.footprint(ticks_per_row = vcFpTicks, va_percent = vcVaPct, imbalance_percent = 300)

if barstate.islast
    polyline.delete(vcPoly)
    line.delete(vcLine)
    label.delete(vcLbl)
    line.delete(vcVahLn)
    line.delete(vcValLn)
    label.delete(vcVahLb)
    label.delete(vcValLb)
    vcPoly  := na
    vcLine  := na
    vcLbl   := na
    vcVahLn := na
    vcValLn := na
    vcVahLb := na
    vcValLb := na
    vcPoc   := na
    vcVah   := na
    vcVal   := na
    vcValid := false

    if vcOn and rangeLive and not na(vcAtr) and vcAtr > 0 and not na(cHiB) and not na(cLoB)
        float vTop = cHi
        float vBot = cLo
        float vH   = vTop - vBot

        if vH > 0
            // row sizing: ATR relative, capped, then re-tiled so the
            // rows span the range exactly
            int vRows = math.max(1, int(math.round(vH / (vcAtr * vcBinMult))))
            if vRows > vcMaxRows
                vRows := vcMaxRows
            float vBin = vH / vRows

            // anchor at the older of the two boundary bars
            int vAnchor = math.min(cHiB, cLoB)
            int vStart  = math.min(math.max(vAnchor, bar_index - vcMaxLook), bar_index)

            bins = array.new<float>(vRows, 0.0)
            int vBars  = 0   // candles in the profile
            int vFpBar = 0   // of which placed from footprint data

            for i = vStart to bar_index
                int   off = bar_index - i
                float bh  = high[off]
                float bl  = low[off]
                float bv  = volume[off]
                // on the CME clock, candles printed while CME was shut
                // carry no volume into the profile
                if onCmeClock and not cmeOpen[off]
                    bv := na
                footprint fb = na
                if vcFpOn and not na(bv)
                    fb := vcFp[off]
                if not na(bh) and not na(bl) and not na(bv) and bv > 0
                    vBars += 1

                if not na(fb)
                    // each footprint row's volume goes to the profile row
                    // holding its midpoint; rows outside the range are not
                    // credited, as with the even spread
                    vFpBar += 1
                    for rw in fb.rows()
                        float rm = (rw.up_price() + rw.down_price()) / 2
                        float rv = rw.buy_volume() + rw.sell_volume()
                        if rm >= vBot and rm <= vTop and rv > 0
                            int ix = math.max(0, math.min(vRows - 1, int(math.floor((rm - vBot) / vBin))))
                            array.set(bins, ix, array.get(bins, ix) + rv)
                else if not na(bh) and not na(bl) and not na(bv) and bv > 0
                    float ch = math.min(bh, vTop)
                    float cl = math.max(bl, vBot)

                    if ch >= cl
                        float span = bh - bl

                        if span <= 0
                            int ix = math.max(0, math.min(vRows - 1, int(math.floor((cl - vBot) / vBin))))
                            array.set(bins, ix, array.get(bins, ix) + bv)
                        else
                            int iLo = math.max(0, math.min(vRows - 1, int(math.floor((cl - vBot) / vBin))))
                            int iHi = math.max(0, math.min(vRows - 1, int(math.floor((ch - vBot) / vBin))))
                            for j = iLo to iHi
                                float rLo = vBot + j * vBin
                                float rHi = rLo + vBin
                                float ov  = math.min(rHi, ch) - math.max(rLo, cl)
                                if ov > 0
                                    array.set(bins, j, array.get(bins, j) + bv * (ov / span))

            float vMax = array.max(bins)

            if not na(vMax) and vMax > 0
                int pocIdx = array.indexof(bins, vMax)
                vcPoc   := vBot + pocIdx * vBin + vBin / 2
                vcValid := true

                // value area: grow from the POC row, each step taking the
                // heavier neighbouring row, until it holds vcVaPct of the
                // volume traded inside the range
                float vSum = array.sum(bins)
                int   vaLo = pocIdx
                int   vaHi = pocIdx
                float vaV  = vMax
                while vaV < vSum * vcVaPct / 100.0 and (vaLo > 0 or vaHi < vRows - 1)
                    float vaUp = vaHi < vRows - 1 ? array.get(bins, vaHi + 1) : -1.0
                    float vaDn = vaLo > 0 ? array.get(bins, vaLo - 1) : -1.0
                    if vaUp >= vaDn
                        vaHi += 1
                        vaV  += vaUp
                    else
                        vaLo -= 1
                        vaV  += vaDn
                vcVah := vBot + (vaHi + 1) * vBin
                vcVal := vBot + vaLo * vBin

                int vX1 = math.min(cHiT, cLoT)
                if vcPocShow
                    string vSrc = not vcFpOn ? "Volume spread evenly across each candle's range." : "Real volume at price on " + str.tostring(vFpBar) + " of " + str.tostring(vBars) + " candles; the rest spread evenly."
                    vcLine := line.new(vX1, vcPoc, xRight, vcPoc, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = vcPocCol, width = vcPocWid, style = line.style_solid)
                    vcLbl  := label.new(xRight, vcPoc, f_label2("POC", vcPoc), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(vcPocCol, 100), textcolor = vcPocCol, size = f_size(lblSize), tooltip = vSrc)

                if vcVaShow
                    vcVahLn := line.new(vX1, vcVah, xRight, vcVah, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = vcVaCol, width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
                    vcValLn := line.new(vX1, vcVal, xRight, vcVal, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = vcVaCol, width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
                    vcVahLb := label.new(xRight, vcVah, f_label2("VAH", vcVah), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(vcVaCol, 100), textcolor = vcVaCol, size = f_size(lblSize))
                    vcValLb := label.new(xRight, vcVal, f_label2("VAL", vcVal), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(vcVaCol, 100), textcolor = vcVaCol, size = f_size(lblSize))

                if vcProfShow
                    // Permanent placement model:
                    //   primary range / P-D box ends at bar_index + extendBars
                    //   widest profile row begins after vcProfGap
                    //   histogram width is controlled independently by vcProfWidth
                    // Keeping gap and width separate prevents a wider profile from
                    // creeping back over candles or into the premium/discount box.
                    int profLeft  = bar_index + extendBars + vcProfGap
                    int profRight = profLeft + vcProfWidth
                    pts = array.new<chart.point>()
                    for k = 0 to vRows - 1
                        float pLo = vBot + k * vBin
                        float pHi = pLo + vBin
                        int   pW  = int(math.round((array.get(bins, k) / vMax) * vcProfWidth))

                        if k == 0
                            array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(profRight, pLo))

                        array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(profRight - pW, pLo))
                        array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(profRight - pW, pHi))

                        if k == vRows - 1
                            array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(profRight, pHi))

                    vcPoly := polyline.new(points = pts, closed = false, line_color = vcProfCol, fill_color = color.new(vcProfCol, vcProfFill), line_width = 1)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Table
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

posTxt    = rangeLive ? (close > wkEq ? "Premium" : close < wkEq ? "Discount" : "Equilibrium") : "—"
sweepSide = lastSweep == 1 ? "Buy-side" : lastSweep == -1 ? "Sell-side" : lastSweep == 2 ? "Both" : "—"
sweepTxt  = sweepSide + (str.length(lastSweepTag) > 0 ? "  " + lastSweepTag : "")
targetTxt = na(drawLvl) ? "—" : fmt_tick(drawLvl) + (drawTag == "" ? "" : "  " + drawTag)

f_od(float p) =>
    od = oddsLbl(p)
    str.length(od) > 0 ? "   " + od : ""

riskTxt = not oddsOn ? "—" : oddsRisk == "Distance to last swing" ? fmt_tick(riskUp) + " ↑ / " + fmt_tick(riskDn) + " ↓" : fmt_tick(riskFlat)
stState  = rangeLive ? "Framed" : primDev ? "Developing" : "None"
stateTxt = (prim == "None" ? "" : primName + " · ") + stState

f_row(table tt, int r, string k, string v) =>
    table.cell(tt, 0, r, k, text_color = tblTxt, text_size = f_tsize(tblSize), text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tt, 1, r, v, text_color = tblTxt, text_size = f_tsize(tblSize), text_halign = text.align_right)

var table t = na
if tblOn and barstate.islast
    table.delete(t)
    t := table.new(f_pos(tblPos), 2, vcOn ? (vcVaShow ? 11 : 10) : 9, bgcolor = tblBg, border_color = tblBorder, border_width = 1, frame_color = tblBorder, frame_width = 1)
    f_row(t, 0, "Range",      stateTxt)
    f_row(t, 1, "Range high", rangeLive ? fmt_tick(cHi) + f_od(cHi) : "—")
    f_row(t, 2, "Range low",  rangeLive ? fmt_tick(cLo) + f_od(cLo) : "—")
    f_row(t, 3, "Delivery",   dlvLive ? fmt_tick(dlv.hi) + " / " + fmt_tick(dlv.lo) : "—")
    f_row(t, 4, "EQ",         fmt_tick(wkEq) + (rangeLive ? f_od(wkEq) : ""))
    f_row(t, 5, "Position",   posTxt)
    f_row(t, 6, "Last sweep", sweepTxt)
    f_row(t, 7, "Draw",       targetTxt + (na(drawLvl) ? "" : f_od(drawLvl)))
    f_row(t, 8, "Risk (1R)",  riskTxt)
    if vcOn
        f_row(t, 9, "POC", vcValid ? fmt_tick(vcPoc) + f_od(vcPoc) : "—")
        if vcVaShow
            f_row(t, 10, "Value area", vcValid ? fmt_tick(vcVah) + " / " + fmt_tick(vcVal) : "—")

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Alerts
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Set in the sweep loop: the exact registered pool that was the draw coming
// into this bar was removed because this bar swept it. A pool cleared by a
// day reset or trimmed by a quota never counts. Confirmed bars only, like
// every other sweep in the tool.
drawHit = drawSwept

alertcondition(firstLive,        "Dealing range framed",   "Dealing range framed")
alertcondition(rangeReframed,    "Dealing range reframed", "Opposing liquidity purged - the working pair changed")
alertcondition(boundaryExtended, "Boundary extended",      "The tracking boundary extended to a new extreme")
alertcondition(drawHit,   "Draw reached",           "Price reached the draw pool")
alertcondition(poolHi,    "BSL swept",              "Buy-side liquidity swept")
alertcondition(poolLo,    "SSL swept",              "Sell-side liquidity swept")
alertcondition(dlvFormed, "Delivery range formed",  "A raid followed by a close through structure formed a delivery range")
alertcondition(frmContracted, "IPDA Frame contracted", "Time event, not a liquidity event: an IPDA Frame boundary aged out of the lookback and moved to the extreme inside the window")
